WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.449 --> 00:00:02.323
(drum music)

00:00:02.323 --> 00:00:04.914
- [Tushar] We break necks all the time.

00:00:04.914 --> 00:00:06.669
It's kind of like the
"deer in the headlights"

00:00:06.669 --> 00:00:09.801
look when they see us
because it's unexpected.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:12.551
(dramatic music)

00:00:14.422 --> 00:00:16.408
(drums)

00:00:16.408 --> 00:00:19.459
A bunch of brown Indian boys
walking down Fifth Avenue

00:00:19.459 --> 00:00:23.052
in New York City in kilts,
you don't see that every day.

00:00:23.052 --> 00:00:25.802
(bagpipes music)

00:00:29.976 --> 00:00:30.945
My name is Tushar Patel.

00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:32.664
I'm a bagpipe player and pipe major for

00:00:32.664 --> 00:00:34.776
Shree Muktajeevan Swamibapa Pipe Band-

00:00:34.776 --> 00:00:36.696
located at Shree Swaminarayan Temple

00:00:36.696 --> 00:00:38.696
in Secaucus, New Jersey.

00:00:40.046 --> 00:00:42.733
(soft music)

00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:46.659
The Shree Swaminarayan religion
is a more modern religion.

00:00:46.659 --> 00:00:50.189
It's a sect of Hinduism
that promotes unity,

00:00:50.189 --> 00:00:52.396
non-violence, and peace and well-being

00:00:52.396 --> 00:00:54.147
all throughout the world.

00:00:54.147 --> 00:00:55.926
(soft music)

00:00:55.926 --> 00:00:58.467
Music is definitely the
fundamental of our faith.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.440
Our spiritual leader, Shree
Muktajeevan Swamibapa,

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.440
loved music.

00:01:02.514 --> 00:01:05.016
He fell in love with the
sound of the bagpipes.

00:01:05.016 --> 00:01:09.656
So, he instructed us to
start our own bagpipe band.

00:01:09.656 --> 00:01:12.323
(bagpipe music)

00:01:14.157 --> 00:01:17.990
No one had any idea how
to play bagpipe music.

00:01:18.915 --> 00:01:20.582
- Not so hard; good.

00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:24.408
- [Tushar] We found online
videos, internet videos,

00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:28.365
we bought a bunch of
intro to bagpipe books.

00:01:28.365 --> 00:01:30.648
We didn't know any music, but we knew that

00:01:30.648 --> 00:01:32.397
if we worked together, if we were unified,

00:01:32.397 --> 00:01:34.917
that we can do anything.

00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:37.334
- By the right, quick, march.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.867
(bagpipe music)

00:01:45.388 --> 00:01:47.745
- The sound of the
bagpipes; it's very similar

00:01:47.745 --> 00:01:51.384
to some instruments
that are found in India.

00:01:51.384 --> 00:01:53.047
While we're playing a Scottish bagpipe,

00:01:53.047 --> 00:01:56.237
we're still playing Indian
music, as well as American music

00:01:56.237 --> 00:01:59.237
and music from all around the world.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.136
(gentle music)

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:06.902
Being here in America, we really wanted

00:02:06.902 --> 00:02:10.835
to blend all the cultures
that our band represents.

00:02:10.835 --> 00:02:12.504
We like to maintain that traditional

00:02:12.504 --> 00:02:14.474
Scottish uniform, but we also like

00:02:14.474 --> 00:02:18.392
to blend in the Indian
and American culture.

00:02:18.392 --> 00:02:21.425
That uniqueness is what defines our band.

00:02:21.425 --> 00:02:23.842
(soft music)

00:02:24.928 --> 00:02:27.768
There's really a sense of pride.

00:02:27.768 --> 00:02:31.171
We're proud of each other, and
proud of where we've grown.

00:02:31.171 --> 00:02:33.688
It's not about only just
playing the bagpipes.

00:02:33.688 --> 00:02:35.928
The reason that we play
is to continue spreading

00:02:35.928 --> 00:02:39.996
our message of peace
and unity through music.

00:02:39.996 --> 00:02:42.579
(gentle music)

